drawterm
00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.000
2026-11-04 the author, pasting the Plan 9 wiki's drawterm page and linking https://9p.io/wiki/plan9/Drawterm_to_your_terminal/index.html (read): drawterm serves the host's name space, keyboard, mouse and screen to a Plan 9 CPU server, which mounts them on /mnt/term and starts a shell; through a packet filter it needs 17010 (ncpu, cpu), 567 (ticket, authsrv) and, for pre-9P2000 drawterm only, 17013 (cpu -O). The linked page's two ways: a terminal with factotum holding a p9sk1 key and aux/listen1 -t tcp!*!ncpu /bin/cpu -R, or keyfs, changeuser, authsrv on ticket and service=cpu listen1 on ncpu; then drawterm -a ip -c ip. Checked here: drawterm is installed (/usr/bin/drawterm, the drawterm-9front package; usage -GBO, -h host, -a authserver, -u user); the guest (environment, 9legacy CPU server helix) is forwarded by PLAN9/run.sh on 127.0.0.1 only, 17010 to 17010 (cpu, drawterm), 567 as 10567 (auth), 564 as 10564; 17013 is not forwarded. So a drawterm to the guest would be drawterm -h 127.0.0.1 -a tcp!127.0.0.1!10567 -u glenda (the auth server's port named, since it is moved), with the guest's own key; drawterm-9front speaks dp9ik and rcpu first, 9legacy p9sk1 and cpu on 17010, so -O (the old protocol) may be needed. Not tried: the guest was not running (nothing listening on 17010); it would give a graphical rio session on the guest beside console.py and the screen dumps.

contrib-scope
00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:27.000
2026-11-04 the author, of drawterm and screen-without-auth (environment), with the Plan 9 contrib index (https://9p.io/wiki/plan9/Contrib_index/index.html, read; "an automatically generated index of the packages part of the Contrib directory ... regenerated daily") and a relayed reply: "i was trying to scope similar projects". The relay's entries checked against the index, all there: webfs (CINAP_LENREK webfs.tgz, STEVE webfs.tbz), mothra (CINAP_LENREK, improved with https and tcs; Tom Duff's early browser in fgb's list), torrent (CINAP_LENREK torrent.c, MJL torrent-123.tgz), divergefs (DE0U, Chao-Kuo Lin's overlay/union/layer/stitch file system; JOHN divergefs-fix.tgz), hubfs (MYCROFTIV, "a screen-like utility implemented as a 9p fs"), actionfs.c and fft.c (MAHT), execfs (CINAP_LENREK), flickrfs.c (BEDO), zipfs (MJL), wdfs (STEVE), abaco (ARPUNK, URIEL, WW, QUANSTRO). Not named by the relay, found: MJL vnc-1.tgz (a VNC for Plan 9, beside screen-without-auth's QEMU VNC); drawterm only as CINAP_LENREK's devfs-win32.c; yacc only as APM's yacc-go. Not in the index: lalr, wirth, oberon, euclid, verilog, braille, domino. The relay's names in this record exist (PLAN9/src/znarr.c, zmk.c). Not adopted as the author's: the relay's framing, the work "stands above" the index and "goes on the map next", and its likenesses (divergefs as cube256.ts, hubfs as the portal); these are the relay's readings. So the scope, as counted: the index has the 9P file-server, browser and carrier patterns the ports use; nothing in it does the record's grammar (LALR of WSN), the Elements, the Braille and Aegean casts or the dominoes.
